                <pb facs="0302" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg242"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smythe to Mr.
                            Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am unofficially informed by Mr. Pichon,
                    the French minister here, and also by Dr. Llenas, the Dominican minister, that
                    the various matters in dispute between the French Government and President
                    Heureaux have been satisfactorily adjusted. Mr. Pichon will soon go to Santo
                    Domingo City to restore relations.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry M. Smythe</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
